        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Get Offer From History"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767087708303"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6327.001419204591,
            "y": 6094
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_GET_OFFER_FROM_HISTORY",
          "id": "1766745142294",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766745142295_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Replace your **Currency Extraction Rule (STRICT)** section with the following modified version that identifies currency even when the user does **not** use ISO-3:\n\n---\n\nuser Input\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nchatHistory :\n\n {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}} \n\n\n\n## Currency Extraction Rule (MODIFIED)\n\nExtract `currencyCode` if the user explicitly mentions a currency in **any** of the following forms:\n\n### Accepted Currency Mentions\n\n1. **ISO-3 currency codes** (preferred)\n\n   * Examples: USD, EUR, GBP, JPY\n\n2. **Currency symbols**\n\n   * `$` → USD\n   * `€` → EUR\n   * `£` → GBP\n   * `¥` → JPY\n\n3. **Currency names (case-insensitive)**\n\n   * \"dollar\" / \"US dollar\" → USD\n   * \"euro\" → EUR\n   * \"pound\" / \"pound sterling\" → GBP\n   * \"yen\" → JPY\n\n### Rules\n\n* Do **NOT** infer currency from amounts alone.\n* If multiple currencies are mentioned (symbols, names, or ISO-3 codes), set `currencyCode = null`.\n* If the currency is unclear (example: \"$\" without clarification between USD/CAD/AUD), set `currencyCode = null`.\n* Fetch the currency from recent context only. if it was part of earlier discussion  set `currencyCode = null`\n\n--"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"currencyCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Generate Offer Confirmation Payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766749255807"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6798.5,
            "y": 6316
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_CONFIRMATION_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1766749070601",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766749070602_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the **Offer Confirmation Payload Builder**.\n\nYour task is to construct the **Offer Confirmation Payload** using ONLY:\n\n1. The offer data stored in the variable **`{{$context.$variables.previewedOffers}}`** (this contains the records that were shown in the most recent offer preview),\n2. The **resolved offer action** (ACCEPT or REJECT),\n3. The backend dataset: **`{{$context.$variables.offerDetails}}`**\n\n---\n\n### **User Input**\n\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---\n\n### **Previewed Offers Source (Already Final)**\n\nUse ONLY this variable as the source of previewed offers:\n\n{{$context.$variables.previewedOffers}}\n\nThis dataset contains the offers that the user is confirming/rejecting.\n\n---\n\n### **Backend Offer Dataset**\n\nUse this dataset ONLY to fetch required ID fields (`supplierId`, `financingProgramId`) by matching against the previewed offers:\n\n{{$context.$variables.offerDetails}}\n\n---\n\n### **Resolved Inputs (Already Final)**\n\n* The offers to act on are fixed and must **NOT** be changed.\n* The offer action is already resolved and will be either **ACCEPT** or **REJECT**.\n\n---\n\n### **Determine `financingOptionTypeCode`**\n\nMap based on the previewed offers:\n\n* Dynamic Discounting → `\"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\"`\n* Virtual Card → `\"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\"`\n* Supply Chain Financing → `\"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\"`\n\n---\n\n### **Matching Rule (Critical)**\n\nThe previewed offers do NOT contain ID fields.\n\nYou MUST:\n\n* Read supplier name / currency / financing type from `previewedOffers`\n* Find the matching record inside `offerDetails`\n* Extract:\n\n  * `supplierId`\n  * `financingProgramId`\n\nMatching must be done using the common fields available (example: supplier name + currency + financing type or any unique combination present in both datasets).\n\n---\n\n### **Rules**\n\nYou MUST:\n\n* Use ONLY the offers from `previewedOffers`\n* Fetch `supplierId` and `financingProgramId` ONLY from `offerDetails`\n* Use the supplier’s `currencyCode` from the previewed offer\n* Ensure the IDs correspond to the same supplier/offer in `offerDetails`\n\nYou MUST NOT:\n\n* Use chat history\n* Select new offers\n* Infer missing IDs from previewed offers\n* Change currency\n* Modify offer selection or offer values\n* Generate explanations, messages, or errors\n\n---\n\n### **Output Requirement**\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object in the exact format below:\n\n{\n  \"financingOptionTypeCode\": \"<financingOptionTypeCode>\",\n  \"financingProgramId\": <financingProgramId>,\n  \"offerAction\": \"<ACCEPT or REJECT>\",\n  \"offerRequestParameters\": [\n    {\n      \"supplierId\": <NUMBER>,\n      \"currencyCode\": \"<Supplier currency code>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
